[agent:result]   Submit a one-time run. This endpoint allows you to submit a workload directly
[agent:result]   without creating a job. Runs submitted using this endpoint don’t display in
[agent:result]   the UI. Use the jobs/runs/get API to check the run state after the job is
[agent:result]   submitted.
[agent:result] 
[agent:result]   **Important:** Jobs submitted using this endpoint are not saved as a job. They
[agent:result]   do not show up in the Jobs UI, and do not retry when they fail. Because they
[agent:result]   are not saved, Databricks cannot auto-optimize serverless compute in case of
[agent:result]   failure. If your job fails, you may want to use classic compute to specify the
[agent:result]   compute needs for the job. Alternatively, use the POST /jobs/create and
[agent:result]   POST /jobs/run-now endpoints to create and run a saved job.
